1
00:00:01,762 --> 00:00:03,222
[theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,981
THE RED IN OUR LIVES

3
00:01:37,233 --> 00:01:39,944
[muffled traffic]

4
00:01:41,695 --> 00:01:45,157
[groans, smacks lips]

5
00:01:47,243 --> 00:01:51,664
[grunting softly]

6
00:01:59,130 --> 00:02:00,422
Uh, Haru?

7
00:02:01,632 --> 00:02:02,633
[sniffs]

8
00:02:05,553 --> 00:02:06,387
[groans softly]

9
00:02:08,931 --> 00:02:09,932
Huh?

10
00:02:10,015 --> 00:02:11,976
[melancholy music playing]

11
00:02:17,148 --> 00:02:18,440
[breath trembles]

12
00:02:21,402 --> 00:02:22,778
[inhales sharply]

13
00:02:22,862 --> 00:02:24,155
[heart beating]

14
00:02:28,242 --> 00:02:30,244
[gasping]

15
00:02:32,496 --> 00:02:33,497
[whimpering]

16
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:38,669
[Legoshi] <i>I'm dreaming, right?
This has gotta be a dream.</i>

17
00:02:39,545 --> 00:02:40,588
Haru...

18
00:02:42,172 --> 00:02:44,174
[sobbing]

19
00:02:46,594 --> 00:02:47,595
This hurts.

20
00:02:49,054 --> 00:02:50,306
This is real.

21
00:02:52,766 --> 00:02:53,642
You idiot!

22
00:02:54,894 --> 00:02:56,854
Why... Why?

23
00:02:57,688 --> 00:03:01,817
[strangled howl]

24
00:03:05,654 --> 00:03:06,655
[inhales sharply]

25
00:03:07,656 --> 00:03:11,243
<i>Haru... Haru.</i>

26
00:03:13,954 --> 00:03:14,830
<i>Haru.</i>

27
00:03:21,003 --> 00:03:22,004
Haru...

28
00:03:23,130 --> 00:03:25,132
[echoing voice] That's how it should be.

29
00:03:26,133 --> 00:03:27,009
Huh?

30
00:03:27,593 --> 00:03:31,722
[shadowy figure] You've buried
your feelings ever since you were a kid.

31
00:03:31,805 --> 00:03:34,391
You've lived quietly in the darkness.

32
00:03:34,934 --> 00:03:38,562
[Legoshi] <i>Hold on.
I thought I had locked you away.</i>

33
00:03:39,855 --> 00:03:44,401
[shadowy figure] Well, it turns out Melon
was kind enough to open the door for me.

34
00:03:44,485 --> 00:03:45,945
[Legoshi gasps]

35
00:03:46,028 --> 00:03:48,489
<i>Those flames
burning deep within his eyes...</i>

36
00:03:49,865 --> 00:03:51,742
<i>It's what I was afraid of.</i>

37
00:03:51,825 --> 00:03:53,577
[sobbing]

38
00:03:53,661 --> 00:03:56,664
[shadowy figure] Don't turn away.
Face yourself.

39
00:03:57,331 --> 00:04:01,210
What feeling creeps in?
Sadness? Or is it frustration?

40
00:04:01,877 --> 00:04:04,004
Or is it neither?

41
00:04:04,088 --> 00:04:07,424
It's your instinct, alive and well.

42
00:04:10,719 --> 00:04:12,554
No! [sobbing]

43
00:04:20,437 --> 00:04:24,692
How could I? What have I done?

44
00:04:26,652 --> 00:04:28,821
<i>I'll never see her again.</i>

45
00:04:28,904 --> 00:04:30,572
[continues sobbing]

46
00:04:33,325 --> 00:04:34,743
[door opens]

47
00:04:34,827 --> 00:04:38,539
[Haru] Oh, sorry about the mess.
I was going to clean that when I got back.

48
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:40,457
Huh?

49
00:04:40,541 --> 00:04:42,918
[sighs] I've gotta be more careful
with tomato juice.

50
00:04:43,002 --> 00:04:45,254
I'm better at spilling it
than drinking it.

51
00:04:45,337 --> 00:04:46,338
H... Haru?

52
00:04:47,298 --> 00:04:48,757
<i>Tomato juice?</i>

53
00:04:48,841 --> 00:04:49,758
[sniffs]

54
00:04:50,342 --> 00:04:52,636
<i>Was I too shocked to use my nose?</i>

55
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,847
[Haru] What is it? What's wrong?

56
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:04,732
Hey, are you okay?
You didn't have a nightmare, did you?

57
00:05:05,858 --> 00:05:09,320
It was a nightmare, and it felt so real.

58
00:05:10,821 --> 00:05:13,324
It was frightening.
I'm just glad I'm awake.

59
00:05:15,034 --> 00:05:17,036
- You're so warm.
- [exhales worriedly]

60
00:05:17,703 --> 00:05:19,955
How about, um, some breakfast?

61
00:05:21,457 --> 00:05:22,791
[chuckles lightly]

62
00:05:24,126 --> 00:05:25,836
We have yogurt and bread.

63
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:29,131
So, which one?
We've got aloe or strawberry.

64
00:05:30,090 --> 00:05:32,551
- [Legoshi sighs]
- Well, for me, I like strawberry.

65
00:05:33,469 --> 00:05:34,970
[Legoshi exhales heavily]

66
00:05:35,054 --> 00:05:36,263
<i>I'm so grateful.</i>

67
00:05:36,346 --> 00:05:39,850
[giggles] Too slow. You get aloe. Here!

68
00:05:39,933 --> 00:05:44,605
[Legoshi] <i>Outside of my nightmare,
I guess we're really pretty lucky.</i>

69
00:05:45,105 --> 00:05:46,148
Come and get it!

70
00:05:46,231 --> 00:05:48,484
[Legoshi] <i>If I have this dream
of eating her...</i>

71
00:05:49,234 --> 00:05:53,405
<i>I can't imagine
Haru hasn't dreamt of me doing it.</i>

72
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:58,786
<i>And yet here she is,
with her yogurt and bread,</i>

73
00:05:58,869 --> 00:06:02,247
<i>happy to have breakfast with me,
like it's just what we do.</i>

74
00:06:03,582 --> 00:06:06,794
<i>You've got all our weight
on your shoulders.</i>

75
00:06:07,503 --> 00:06:10,964
<i>Just you. But because of that, we work.</i>

76
00:06:11,715 --> 00:06:13,217
- Listen, Haru!
- [Haru exclaims]

77
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:14,384
[gentle music playing]

78
00:06:14,468 --> 00:06:15,302
You and me...

79
00:06:16,011 --> 00:06:17,888
I think you and I should get married.

80
00:06:18,388 --> 00:06:21,475
I wanna live with you. Maybe have kids.

81
00:06:21,558 --> 00:06:25,187
And no matter what nightmares pop up,
I know we can handle it.

82
00:06:25,270 --> 00:06:28,232
And I wanna have yogurt
every single day with you.

83
00:06:29,066 --> 00:06:32,736
I mean, don't we deserve happiness?
I wanna be happy with you.

84
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:34,988
Uh... yeah.

85
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:39,576
Okay. Well, then, I have a request for us.

86
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:41,203
[Legoshi] Anything.

87
00:06:41,286 --> 00:06:43,413
I wanna see the Festival of the Meteor.

88
00:06:44,123 --> 00:06:45,415
And I wanna go with you.

89
00:06:46,708 --> 00:06:47,835
The festival?

90
00:06:47,918 --> 00:06:49,878
Well, we couldn't do it last year.

91
00:06:50,504 --> 00:06:53,674
And when we go,
let's light a candle together.

92
00:06:54,883 --> 00:06:55,884
Make a promise.

93
00:07:02,224 --> 00:07:04,101
[Legoshi] <i>She will be my wife.</i>

94
00:07:05,144 --> 00:07:09,273
<i>Before that, though,
I made a promise to Mr. Yahya.</i>

95
00:07:12,317 --> 00:07:14,027
<i>Where are you, Melon?</i>

96
00:07:14,111 --> 00:07:15,571
[music swells forebodingly]

97
00:07:15,654 --> 00:07:18,907
KING OF BEASTS

98
00:07:18,991 --> 00:07:19,992
[Free sighs]

99
00:07:20,951 --> 00:07:22,703
You know, Melon, he, uh...

100
00:07:22,786 --> 00:07:25,205
he never even bothered
to learn Hino's name.

101
00:07:26,707 --> 00:07:31,128
And in Melon's eyes, gang members are
nothing but weak little pawns.

102
00:07:33,297 --> 00:07:34,506
HERE LIES HINO

103
00:07:34,590 --> 00:07:35,549
[Agata] Damn, Hino...

104
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:40,012
You deserved better. You deserved a death
worthy of a lion's mane.

105
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:42,931
[clippers buzzing]

106
00:07:43,474 --> 00:07:44,766
Hey! What are you doing?

107
00:07:44,850 --> 00:07:46,935
I haven't earned my mane, have I?

108
00:07:47,436 --> 00:07:50,314
I'm following Melon
even after Hino was killed.

109
00:07:50,397 --> 00:07:51,940
The king of beasts, my ass!

110
00:07:52,024 --> 00:07:53,400
- Stop! Come on!
- [all struggling]

111
00:07:53,484 --> 00:07:54,568
I don't deserve this mane!

112
00:07:54,651 --> 00:07:56,695
- Stop! Just stop!
- Get off me! Just let me do this!

113
00:07:56,778 --> 00:07:58,489
We're right here with you!

114
00:07:58,572 --> 00:08:00,991
- We know this isn't easy!
- Remember what he said!

115
00:08:01,074 --> 00:08:03,744
He said, since you were born a male lion,

116
00:08:03,827 --> 00:08:07,623
it falls upon you to become
a king of beasts worthy of your mane.

117
00:08:07,706 --> 00:08:10,042
Exactly. You take care of it
until you earn it,

118
00:08:10,125 --> 00:08:12,336
and that takes time. And you know that.

119
00:08:13,170 --> 00:08:15,422
But Hino... our Hino...

120
00:08:17,466 --> 00:08:21,178
At this rate, my mane will just sit
on the head of a pretender!

121
00:08:21,261 --> 00:08:22,179
[inhales shakily]

122
00:08:23,222 --> 00:08:25,599
{\an8}How am I supposed to ever forgive Melon?

123
00:08:25,682 --> 00:08:27,643
{\an8}He'll never be Shishi-Gumi!

124
00:08:28,435 --> 00:08:30,187
[Victor] Are you gonna
take him down, then?

125
00:08:31,146 --> 00:08:33,065
And you think you're up for that?

126
00:08:33,148 --> 00:08:36,026
Let's say you do.
When a turf war breaks out,

127
00:08:36,109 --> 00:08:38,362
what are we supposed to do without a boss?

128
00:08:38,445 --> 00:08:40,030
Meat Appreciation Day...

129
00:08:40,113 --> 00:08:42,616
How great would it be
if we got Louis back?

130
00:08:42,699 --> 00:08:44,201
Yeah, that'd be nice.

131
00:08:44,284 --> 00:08:48,539
Louis, huh... He treated us
like the kings of beasts that we are.

132
00:08:49,331 --> 00:08:52,834
That was great.
I'll admit, Louis was the man.

133
00:08:52,918 --> 00:08:54,461
But nothing lasts forever.

134
00:08:54,545 --> 00:08:57,256
Well, if we asked nicely,
he might come back.

135
00:08:57,339 --> 00:09:00,467
- Maybe if we bowed our heads in respect--
- [Legoshi] No way! You can't do that!

136
00:09:00,551 --> 00:09:01,468
- What?
- The hell?

137
00:09:01,552 --> 00:09:02,427
[Legoshi] Oh.

138
00:09:02,511 --> 00:09:05,138
- [Free] Looky here. I remember you.
- [guns cock]

139
00:09:05,222 --> 00:09:07,349
Looks like you're still alive.

140
00:09:07,432 --> 00:09:10,185
What are you doing here?
Forget what dyin' feels like?

141
00:09:10,269 --> 00:09:11,353
[Legoshi] You gotta listen.

142
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:14,648
Hear me out. I just...
just want to ask something.

143
00:09:14,731 --> 00:09:15,732
[lion snarls]

144
00:09:15,816 --> 00:09:18,151
I want Melon,
and I thought you all could help.

145
00:09:18,235 --> 00:09:20,821
- And why would you think that?
- I want to catch him.

146
00:09:21,446 --> 00:09:24,449
Unless I'm wrong,
sounds like you all want Melon gone.

147
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,868
If we could work toge-- Whoa!

148
00:09:27,703 --> 00:09:30,163
Us following a wolf? You must be nuts!

149
00:09:30,247 --> 00:09:32,374
[Legoshi] I'm not asking you to follow me.

150
00:09:32,457 --> 00:09:34,835
Now, wait. We seem to have the same goal.

151
00:09:35,586 --> 00:09:38,088
Louis is my senior,
but I don't think he should be your boss.

152
00:09:38,171 --> 00:09:41,466
What? What do you mean,
Louis is your senior?

153
00:09:42,092 --> 00:09:44,595
- What are you blabbing about?
- In high school he was my senior.

154
00:09:44,678 --> 00:09:45,679
[Jimma] Huh?

155
00:09:45,762 --> 00:09:47,889
I don't care who you are to Louis.

156
00:09:47,973 --> 00:09:49,391
[Victor grunts]

157
00:09:49,474 --> 00:09:51,977
Yeah, sure, Melon's a problem for us,

158
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:54,605
but we're not desperate enough
to turn to a canine!

159
00:09:54,688 --> 00:09:57,566
Don't worry, pup.
We can solve this on our own.

160
00:09:57,649 --> 00:10:00,402
And now, since those canine ears
hear so well,

161
00:10:00,485 --> 00:10:02,529
now we gotta make sure you stay dead!

162
00:10:03,030 --> 00:10:04,698
[Legoshi grunting]

163
00:10:08,410 --> 00:10:09,995
[Legoshi panting]

164
00:10:12,456 --> 00:10:13,582
Use your heads.

165
00:10:14,166 --> 00:10:16,543
You think Louis will forgive you
if you kill me?

166
00:10:16,627 --> 00:10:18,629
Pretty confident, I see.

167
00:10:18,712 --> 00:10:20,714
I'll admit, kid, you got balls.

168
00:10:20,797 --> 00:10:23,800
But losing any more of our lion's pride
ain't on the table.

169
00:10:25,552 --> 00:10:28,138
This time when you die, you'll stay dead.

170
00:10:28,722 --> 00:10:30,432
[growls]

171
00:10:31,892 --> 00:10:33,977
- [Mayor] <i>The Zoolympics.</i>
- [triumphant music playing]

172
00:10:34,061 --> 00:10:36,146
[Mayor] <i>All manner of species
coming together</i>

173
00:10:36,229 --> 00:10:38,899
<i>to showcase a wide range
of special abilities.</i>

174
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:42,152
<i>It's an event
that transcends our differences,</i>

175
00:10:42,235 --> 00:10:46,031
where we can exist in peace
and mutually appreciate our achievements.

176
00:10:46,865 --> 00:10:50,035
{\an8}It embodies our slogan, "Live Together,"

177
00:10:50,118 --> 00:10:52,788
{\an8}my vision for co-existence and prosperity.

178
00:10:54,164 --> 00:10:59,044
I'm currently considering the prospect of
bringing the Zoolympics to our fine city.

179
00:10:59,127 --> 00:11:02,673
Interesting. I've heard
the costs can be astronomical.

180
00:11:03,215 --> 00:11:05,801
Oftentimes, cities withdraw their bids.

181
00:11:05,884 --> 00:11:09,429
In spite of that,
I believe there's an opportunity there.

182
00:11:09,513 --> 00:11:12,891
As for the costs, I'm a little more
optimistic in that regard.

183
00:11:12,974 --> 00:11:16,603
Of course, that depends on Mr. Ogma
chairing the bidding committee.

184
00:11:16,686 --> 00:11:17,729
{\an8}MAYOR

185
00:11:17,813 --> 00:11:21,316
{\an8}[Louis] <i>Something seems off here.
Does Father have some kind of a plan?</i>

186
00:11:22,067 --> 00:11:24,736
{\an8}[Mayor] On top of that,
I feel we have something special

187
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:26,488
we can bring to the table.

188
00:11:29,241 --> 00:11:31,159
[Louis] Uh... raw meat?

189
00:11:31,243 --> 00:11:32,828
[Mayor] Lab-cultured meat.

190
00:11:32,911 --> 00:11:36,248
Oh, yeah, I vaguely recall
hearing about that.

191
00:11:36,331 --> 00:11:38,250
[Mayor] Using cultured muscle cells,

192
00:11:38,333 --> 00:11:41,420
this was artificially created
through the wonders of science,

193
00:11:42,212 --> 00:11:46,758
meaning no one had to die for this
and it can be consumed ethically.

194
00:11:46,842 --> 00:11:49,803
[Louis] Its resemblance to the real thing
is remarkable.

195
00:11:49,886 --> 00:11:52,806
[Mayor] It tastes like regular meat
and has the same nutrients.

196
00:11:53,390 --> 00:11:55,434
I didn't know its development
was this far along.

197
00:11:55,976 --> 00:11:58,145
Apparently, it's almost ready for release.

198
00:11:58,895 --> 00:11:59,771
[Louis] So then...

199
00:12:00,272 --> 00:12:04,443
It's no secret some athletes have been
eating meat and getting away with it,

200
00:12:04,526 --> 00:12:06,903
and that's, of course,
a regrettable aspect.

201
00:12:06,987 --> 00:12:07,904
Agreed.

202
00:12:07,988 --> 00:12:12,701
So, then, what if the solution is
offering this meat to those same athletes?

203
00:12:12,784 --> 00:12:15,954
I'm sure carnivores across the board
would have no problem with that.

204
00:12:16,037 --> 00:12:19,332
And with that, its nutrition
would give them the edge

205
00:12:19,416 --> 00:12:21,209
for record-breaking performance.

206
00:12:22,043 --> 00:12:24,504
For Horns Pharmaceuticals and Ogura Foods,

207
00:12:24,588 --> 00:12:27,883
it's the perfect advertising opportunity.

208
00:12:28,508 --> 00:12:32,762
[Louis] <i>So, Azuki's father's company,
working with Horns Pharmaceuticals?</i>

209
00:12:32,846 --> 00:12:33,972
<i>This smells fishy.</i>

210
00:12:34,639 --> 00:12:37,559
- [Louis gasps]
- [Mayor] So here's where you come in.

211
00:12:38,101 --> 00:12:41,897
We have decided that you should serve
as our ambassador for the bid.

212
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:42,898
[Louis] What?

213
00:12:42,981 --> 00:12:46,067
The younger crowds respect you.
You have influence.

214
00:12:46,151 --> 00:12:48,945
You're seen as a future Beastar
by the community.

215
00:12:49,029 --> 00:12:50,280
[Louis exhales tensely]

216
00:12:50,864 --> 00:12:51,948
Uh, Father?

217
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:54,743
I think it's clear.

218
00:12:56,244 --> 00:12:57,329
I understand.

219
00:12:59,289 --> 00:13:00,457
- [phone buzzes]
- Oh.

220
00:13:03,084 --> 00:13:05,629
[Mayor] Oh, look at how your antlers
have grown.

221
00:13:05,712 --> 00:13:07,255
KITTY:
WE'VE GOT THE WOLF

222
00:13:07,339 --> 00:13:09,382
Like father, like son.

223
00:13:10,467 --> 00:13:12,552
I'm looking forward to working together.

224
00:13:14,971 --> 00:13:18,391
All right, let's start
the first read-through. We ready?

225
00:13:18,475 --> 00:13:20,644
[all affirm]

226
00:13:21,228 --> 00:13:24,439
[Juno] <i>Pina, you really know
how to get under my skin,</i>

227
00:13:24,523 --> 00:13:26,525
<i>but for the sake of the play,
I can look past that.</i>

228
00:13:26,608 --> 00:13:28,193
[Kibi] "One thousand years ago,

229
00:13:28,276 --> 00:13:31,988
an era when herbivores and carnivores
lived together in harmony,

230
00:13:32,072 --> 00:13:33,114
without division..."

231
00:13:33,198 --> 00:13:35,909
"Laila and the others went out
to gather fruit."

232
00:13:35,992 --> 00:13:38,203
"It's been seven sunrises
since they left."

233
00:13:38,286 --> 00:13:40,413
"They don't usually take this long."

234
00:13:40,497 --> 00:13:43,542
"Don't worry, it's Laila.
She's definitely fine."

235
00:13:43,625 --> 00:13:46,169
"Laila enters from stage right."

236
00:13:47,337 --> 00:13:50,048
"Everyone, don't worry. We've returned!"

237
00:13:50,131 --> 00:13:53,051
"On our way back
we were attacked by Jaguars,

238
00:13:53,134 --> 00:13:55,428
but with these fangs, and with my claws--"

239
00:13:55,512 --> 00:13:57,305
"Everyone, don't worry. We've returned!"

240
00:13:57,389 --> 00:13:59,975
"On our way back we were attacked
by Jaguars, but with--"

241
00:14:00,058 --> 00:14:02,227
Whoa, hold it, hang on!
What are you doing?

242
00:14:02,310 --> 00:14:03,770
Stick to the lines that are yours.

243
00:14:03,853 --> 00:14:08,066
I understand the concept.
I was just thinking how I would play it.

244
00:14:08,149 --> 00:14:09,150
Huh?

245
00:14:09,985 --> 00:14:13,780
The character is a strong leader
with a quiet confidence.

246
00:14:13,864 --> 00:14:17,367
Wouldn't it be striking
if they're nonchalant about this violence?

247
00:14:17,450 --> 00:14:20,120
- Oh, yeah, I see what you mean.
- Yeah, but--

248
00:14:20,203 --> 00:14:25,000
Okay, you're only here for one reason.
You're perfect for the role of Garan.

249
00:14:25,083 --> 00:14:28,211
That's right. Let's remember
the illustrations of herbivores

250
00:14:28,295 --> 00:14:30,422
from the time period this play is set in.

251
00:14:30,505 --> 00:14:32,507
The horned sheep is very iconic.

252
00:14:32,591 --> 00:14:36,011
With you in that role, we bring in
the authentic flavor of that era.

253
00:14:36,094 --> 00:14:38,763
[Pina] Mmm, yeah, I hear you
about that ancient stuff.

254
00:14:39,723 --> 00:14:44,519
Listen. Wouldn't me playing a carnivore
be more intriguing?

255
00:14:44,603 --> 00:14:45,729
[Kibi] You're saying...

256
00:14:45,812 --> 00:14:48,273
Imagine this. We shake things up.

257
00:14:48,356 --> 00:14:51,192
The carnivores and herbivores
swap their roles.

258
00:14:51,276 --> 00:14:52,277
- Huh?
- Hmmm?

259
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:55,906
{\an8}Isn't that... Isn't that
a little bit out there? [chuckles]

260
00:14:55,989 --> 00:14:59,200
Ugh! Classic behavior
of an egotistical narcissist!

261
00:14:59,284 --> 00:15:01,494
{\an8}Won't that just confuse the audience?

262
00:15:01,578 --> 00:15:04,748
I get that, but we could find some ways
to make it more clear,

263
00:15:04,831 --> 00:15:06,416
like using wardrobe to spell it out.

264
00:15:07,042 --> 00:15:10,503
{\an8}Not bad. Maybe we could dress
the herbivores in green,

265
00:15:10,587 --> 00:15:12,714
{\an8}and then the carnivores could wear orange.

266
00:15:12,797 --> 00:15:15,675
{\an8}Isn't an aspect of acting
the valiant attempt

267
00:15:15,759 --> 00:15:17,510
to portray something you are not?

268
00:15:17,594 --> 00:15:21,181
- Well, yeah, you do have a point...
- Now, wait just a second!

269
00:15:24,309 --> 00:15:28,188
You've got some nerve! You want to steal
the role of Laila from me.

270
00:15:28,772 --> 00:15:31,858
Besides, I don't know the first thing
about playing an herbivore.

271
00:15:31,942 --> 00:15:34,819
That's perfect, then.
You can challenge yourself.

272
00:15:34,903 --> 00:15:37,989
Playing Laila is already
challenging enough!

273
00:15:38,073 --> 00:15:39,741
Has it even occurred to you

274
00:15:39,824 --> 00:15:42,118
that you don't understand
the carnivore experience?

275
00:15:42,202 --> 00:15:45,830
Let me ask you, Juno, have you ever caused
harm to an herbivore before?

276
00:15:45,914 --> 00:15:46,831
What?

277
00:15:47,415 --> 00:15:49,751
Have you ever hurt one, or eaten one?

278
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:53,254
- Anything like that?
- [Juno] No, of course I haven't.

279
00:15:53,338 --> 00:15:56,967
So when your character does those things,
you're using your imagination?

280
00:15:57,050 --> 00:15:58,885
Yeah, but that's not the same.

281
00:15:58,969 --> 00:16:00,303
[Pina] I understand, Juno.

282
00:16:00,387 --> 00:16:04,015
You just want the role that shows you
in your best light, am I right?

283
00:16:04,891 --> 00:16:08,520
A role with just enough drama,
and monologues,

284
00:16:08,603 --> 00:16:11,690
so you can soak up the spotlight
as the glamorous protagonist.

285
00:16:11,773 --> 00:16:13,817
You're wrong! It's about the play.

286
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:16,861
I just want to serve the work, and play
the role that I'm the best fit for.

287
00:16:16,945 --> 00:16:20,281
I believe in you. That's why I think
you should play an herbivore.

288
00:16:21,074 --> 00:16:22,784
You wanna be a Beastar, right?

289
00:16:22,867 --> 00:16:25,662
- Just think, looks good on a résumé...
- My résumé?

290
00:16:25,745 --> 00:16:28,623
Can you imagine it?
You playing a weak herbivore

291
00:16:28,707 --> 00:16:30,834
who can only survive by acting tough.

292
00:16:31,501 --> 00:16:33,086
I can almost see it now.

293
00:16:33,712 --> 00:16:35,463
- That could work.
- Yeah.

294
00:16:35,547 --> 00:16:37,674
There's nothing wrong
with playing it safe.

295
00:16:37,757 --> 00:16:39,009
At least it would be easier.

296
00:16:39,092 --> 00:16:41,177
[Kibi] Yeah,
but now that I think about it,

297
00:16:41,261 --> 00:16:43,096
Pina might be on to something.

298
00:16:43,179 --> 00:16:44,723
I have to say, it sounds good.

299
00:16:45,265 --> 00:16:47,308
Pina's got some great ideas.

300
00:16:47,392 --> 00:16:49,894
Sounds like it can make the theme
really stand out.

301
00:16:49,978 --> 00:16:52,647
Also, it kind of connects back to Adler.

302
00:16:52,731 --> 00:16:57,235
<i>Isn't it true that Adler originally had
herbivores playing predators</i>

303
00:16:57,318 --> 00:16:59,029
<i>to reinforce his ideas?</i>

304
00:16:59,112 --> 00:17:03,575
Well, I must admit, it would make
the dual performance more meaningful,

305
00:17:03,658 --> 00:17:06,077
- and much more unique...
- You aren't being serious!

306
00:17:06,161 --> 00:17:09,330
[Pina laughs]
Does the prospect of this frighten you?

307
00:17:10,165 --> 00:17:12,876
Are you worried because you don't think
you can pull it off?

308
00:17:12,959 --> 00:17:15,545
What? I can't believe you.

309
00:17:15,628 --> 00:17:18,298
What makes you think stepping into
the role of a carnivore is easy?

310
00:17:18,381 --> 00:17:21,301
I actually think
it'll be quite the challenge,

311
00:17:21,384 --> 00:17:23,344
one I know I'm ready for.

312
00:17:24,512 --> 00:17:26,848
Well, all right. I'll do it.

313
00:17:27,682 --> 00:17:29,350
I'll play Garan, then!

314
00:17:29,434 --> 00:17:31,978
You'll be sorry, 'cause I'll do it
better than you ever could.

315
00:17:32,062 --> 00:17:35,356
Nice! That's the spirit.

316
00:17:36,441 --> 00:17:37,525
[Juno sighs]

317
00:17:37,609 --> 00:17:39,778
<i>What am I getting myself into?</i>

318
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:49,996
[line ringing]

319
00:17:52,332 --> 00:17:53,208
[Louis] I'm here.

320
00:17:58,838 --> 00:18:00,423
So, how's the hostage?

321
00:18:00,507 --> 00:18:02,300
I wondered if you'd come.

322
00:18:02,842 --> 00:18:04,177
You've got some nerve.

323
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:07,764
What part of threatening me
sounded like a good idea?

324
00:18:07,847 --> 00:18:10,475
Tell me another way
we could have gotten you to show up.

325
00:18:10,558 --> 00:18:13,228
You know it's true.
You won't even pick up the phone.

326
00:18:13,311 --> 00:18:15,355
Enough. Just bring out the wolf.

327
00:18:15,438 --> 00:18:18,024
If you hurt them,
then we're gonna have a problem.

328
00:18:18,108 --> 00:18:19,234
[Louis stifles exclamation]

329
00:18:19,317 --> 00:18:21,444
You're kidding me. You're the wolf?

330
00:18:21,528 --> 00:18:23,613
So, uh, hello... Oh!

331
00:18:24,322 --> 00:18:27,742
[Louis sighs exasperatedly]
What the hell are you doing here?

332
00:18:27,826 --> 00:18:31,412
[chuckles awkwardly] Let me guess.
Did you think it was Juno they took?

333
00:18:31,496 --> 00:18:32,997
[Louis sighs]

334
00:18:33,081 --> 00:18:34,499
So, tell me what happened.

335
00:18:35,083 --> 00:18:38,711
{\an8}I need to talk to Melon,
and I figured they knew where he was.

336
00:18:38,795 --> 00:18:41,798
{\an8}If I recall, you were done with Melon.
Isn't that right?

337
00:18:41,881 --> 00:18:44,467
{\an8}Yeah, I was, but, well...

338
00:18:44,551 --> 00:18:48,096
if I can catch Melon, they'll erase
my carnivore criminal record.

339
00:18:48,888 --> 00:18:51,766
If I don't, I won't be able to marry Haru.

340
00:18:53,893 --> 00:18:56,771
So your bright idea was to get them
to tell you where Melon was?

341
00:18:57,397 --> 00:18:58,898
You know they could have killed you.

342
00:18:58,982 --> 00:19:01,568
Well, "could have" almost became "did,"

343
00:19:01,651 --> 00:19:04,487
although they did say
if you asked them, they'd tell me.

344
00:19:04,571 --> 00:19:07,949
The way he was saying it was that
you'd show up if it was for him.

345
00:19:08,616 --> 00:19:10,702
- What?
- [laughing nervously] Well...

346
00:19:10,785 --> 00:19:14,914
I know you cut ties with the Shishi-Gumi,
so this is on me. I'm sorry.

347
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:18,668
Uh, but still, though,
think you could do me a solid?

348
00:19:18,751 --> 00:19:20,003
Jeez...

349
00:19:20,712 --> 00:19:23,506
Even if you caught this mixed maniac,

350
00:19:23,590 --> 00:19:25,884
that's no guarantee
of a happily ever after.

351
00:19:26,551 --> 00:19:28,803
Right. I'll keep that in mind.

352
00:19:31,723 --> 00:19:33,099
[footsteps echoing heavily]

353
00:19:41,816 --> 00:19:43,276
I'm here, as you asked.

354
00:19:44,277 --> 00:19:47,405
Tell him where Melon is.
Make good on your end.

355
00:19:48,239 --> 00:19:51,701
[Dolph] Sure, we're gonna tell him,
on one condition.

356
00:19:51,784 --> 00:19:52,619
Which is...

357
00:19:53,536 --> 00:19:54,704
Louis...

358
00:19:55,496 --> 00:19:57,749
we want you to take up the mantle again.

359
00:19:57,832 --> 00:20:00,210
Come back and be our Shishi-Gumi boss.

360
00:20:00,293 --> 00:20:02,378
- Stop it. That's not fair!
- [Dolph] Quiet!

361
00:20:03,046 --> 00:20:06,466
- We'll follow your orders if you lead us.
- [Legoshi] This wasn't our agreement.

362
00:20:06,549 --> 00:20:08,051
So if you want us to help this wolf...

363
00:20:08,134 --> 00:20:10,220
[Legoshi] You said if he asked,
that would be enough.

364
00:20:10,303 --> 00:20:11,346
- Shut it!
- [Legoshi] Sorry.

365
00:20:11,429 --> 00:20:12,680
That's all we ask.

366
00:20:13,514 --> 00:20:16,517
- [inhales deeply] So we're clear?
- [moody jazz music playing]

367
00:20:16,601 --> 00:20:18,603
You'll help him if I take the reins?

368
00:20:20,855 --> 00:20:23,858
Respectfully... We're begging you.

369
00:20:30,573 --> 00:20:32,784
[Legoshi] <i>I've never seen
anything like this.</i>

370
00:20:33,952 --> 00:20:38,873
<i>Look at him.
A deer that is able to command lions.</i>

371
00:20:41,542 --> 00:20:42,669
I refuse.

372
00:20:43,378 --> 00:20:46,464
- Huh?
- But... why not?

373
00:20:48,341 --> 00:20:49,342
[Louis sighs softly]

374
00:20:49,968 --> 00:20:51,803
Ibuki died because of me...

375
00:20:53,346 --> 00:20:55,723
and because I said
I would step down as boss.

376
00:20:55,807 --> 00:20:58,059
[Free sighs]

377
00:20:58,851 --> 00:21:00,353
[Louis] I can't forget that.

378
00:21:01,521 --> 00:21:05,942
He gave his life. He died
to protect the Shishi-Gumi's pride.

379
00:21:12,865 --> 00:21:15,785
And if I returned,
his death would be for nothing.

380
00:21:16,828 --> 00:21:17,662
Therefore...

381
00:21:18,204 --> 00:21:22,500
I can't return.
I can never be your boss again.

382
00:21:23,918 --> 00:21:25,878
[footsteps echoing heavily]

383
00:21:27,547 --> 00:21:29,090
Louis... [sighs softly]

384
00:21:32,677 --> 00:21:35,346
I'm sorry. I hope you understand.

385
00:21:35,888 --> 00:21:37,432
[Legoshi sighs]

386
00:21:43,855 --> 00:21:44,939
[Free] Hey.

387
00:21:45,023 --> 00:21:45,857
Huh?

388
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:47,734
So, about Melon...

389
00:21:47,817 --> 00:21:51,279
Apparently he's called "Professor"
in polite society.

390
00:21:52,363 --> 00:21:53,489
Oh.

391
00:21:56,451 --> 00:21:57,827
"Professor"?

392
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:03,541
[closing theme song playing]
